# SAVE - Write memory pages to a file

```text
SAVE pages filespec
```

SAVE writes from 0100H in 256-byte pages. The page count is decimal. For
example, after loading a 512-byte program with [GET](GET.HLP), this
command saves two pages on D:

```text
SAVE 2 D0:NEW.COM
```

Choose the page count to cover the intended bytes. Extra pages copy
whatever follows the image in memory.
